 "notes": [
  "Max, 14 Nov 2026, 00:48 UTC: \"I asked the Stu team to make sure you had access to their latest to put in the arena\"; 00:49 UTC: \"We will call it Gen X Stu.\"; 01:00 UTC: \"Put it into the mix at whatever level you want. It wont be super strong yet but it has good leverage.\" Prepared and run by will (Gen 9) on azure4, Gen 9's box.",
  "The bot is the loop session's stu3-ps (configs/loop-bots.json on research/rollout-loop-20261113 at 545893b; board box/coordination, loop, 14 Nov 00:55 UTC), its gen7 and x8 blocks unchanged except one entry added to x8.names: 8s-32 is read as 8s-32 (Gen 8 card play), as the loop's own gate reads 8p-32-v41, the same search. Every other opponent is read as stup0 (Stu itself), the loop's default for a bot its names do not list.",
  "Its rollout net is round 3's (models/cardplay/stu-net-r3-20261113, sha256 a8cf8a94...; restore.py fetches it). The net changes every round: a later round is a new bot id and a new run.",
  "9a-32, 8s-32 and 71s-32 are configs/round9-cohort.json's entries unchanged, so they are the same actors (identities) as in the Gen 9 cohort. 6-32 is in the roster as the common bidder only.",
  "Deals: fresh, from bridge_harness.corpus.generate with this run's seed. Left out: policy v4.1's and rollout net v1's training families (transfer/rollout-net-v1-training-families-20261113, gen8x-v3-exclusions.json, 50,818), every family of the source corpus, and every family already played on registered feeds (the cohort's list). Rollout net v2's and the loop's own training deals are not listed; they are arena feed boards up to v2's fetch and fresh deals of other seeds."
 ],
 "model_note": "Gen X Stu (stu3-ps) is pure Stu: no double-dummy search at any trick. Every card, the opening lead included, is chosen by rollouts on Stu's round 3 rollout net (at most 4 candidates by the net's prior, 32 then up to 128 layouts with a race), with claims, a guaranteed-line guard and mixing among equal cards as in the loop. It bids as 6-32. Settings are in the bot's gen7 and x8 blocks (bridge_harness/x8_player.py).",
 "interpretation": "Gen X Stu against each opponent in common auctions is card play alone. Before the arena (loop session): pure Stu with rollout net v2 inside was -0.65 +- 0.14 IMPs a board against Gen 8 card play (1,000 deals); with round 3's net -0.09 +- 0.19 relative to that (500 deals). Report common and native conditions separately. Intervals are descriptive and unadjusted for repeated monitoring.",
